model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Only a moving-head read failure schedules a reconfirmation timer, at one, three and nine seconds with a shared three-reconfirm cap. Heartbeats and handshakes can also reconfirm; stream signals, activity changes, manual retry and unmount cancel pending timers. Healthy watches schedule no recovery timer; the global heartbeat remains at fifteen seconds. Every reconfirm uses the unchanged authoritative before/body/after fence and principal binding. Never-settling heads remain fail-closed, healthy idle signals cause no head or body read, and an explicit retry remains available after the automatic budget ends. UI copy, layout, and the real first-entry overlap assertions and deadlines stay unchanged."
    }
  }
}
